From t.jombart at imperial.ac.uk  Sun Aug  2 19:31:00 2009
From: t.jombart at imperial.ac.uk (Jombart, Thibaut)
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2009 18:31:00 +0100
Subject: [Phylobase-devl] Aug. virtual hackathon
In-Reply-To: <367E121A-B642-42A3-946C-AD2B2EA3CC34@gmail.com>
References: <FEE6C123-9A7B-4235-ADB6-E1D21BA6F3EE@berkeley.edu>
	<4A749CF1.7090007@ufl.edu>,
	<367E121A-B642-42A3-946C-AD2B2EA3CC34@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <0B75A6276180B546A1CA8D2B46E7580502FB9EF36D@ICEXM3.ic.ac.uk>

Congratulations Brian for your new position!

I'll be off and far from a computer from 4th to 25th August, so I could help to hack our way onto CRAN starting from the 26th. I'm very pleased to think we're getting close to a first release on CRAN. I think a stable release is essential to allow the existence of other packages which would depend on phylobase for data representation/handling, which was one of the original aim of the package. Actually, I have a young adephylo package, which will ultimately (and hopefully soon) replace all phylogenetic functions in ade4, and uses phylo4/phylo4d classes, that desperately waits for a stable phylobase to become a grown-up package.

Thanks for making things move forward again.

Best,

Thibaut.

 
     
